SYSINFO(2)                     P32W Unix                      SYSINFO(2)

NAME
       sysinfo - get system statistics

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/sysinfo.h>

       int sysinfo(struct sysinfo *info);

              struct sysinfo {
                  unsigned uptime;            /* seconds since boot */
                  unsigned totalram, freeram; /* bytes */
                  unsigned procs;             /* processes */
                  unsigned loads[3];          /* load averages x 2048 */
                  unsigned tlbrefills;        /* since boot */
                  unsigned cowcopies;
                  unsigned stackpages;
              };

DESCRIPTION
       sysinfo fills *info with: the seconds since the system
       started; the RAM available for the kernel and processes
       (8 MiB) and how much of it is free, in bytes; the number of
       processes, zombies included; and the load average, the
       number of runnable processes averaged over the last 1, 5
       and 15 minutes, times 2048 (sampled every 5 seconds); and,
       since boot, the TLB refills (user pages loaded into the TLB
       on a miss), the copy-on-write page copies and the stack
       pages added.

       The library passes the structure's size to the kernel, which
       fills no more than that, so programs built before the last
       three fields were added still work.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success; -1 on an error, with errno set.

ERRORS
       EFAULT  info is a bad address.

SEE ALSO
       uptime(1), top(1), pinfo(2), times(2)

BUGS
       It is P32W's own; Linux has a sysinfo with a different
       structure.
